{"id":"43e59272-8cf6-4efd-8b59-54006c2f3baa","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c987c4e2850e5c02","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/git-refs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"eef8b788164026057689f0e0c310f09d89d2f21d","start":2674,"end":2756},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","DOCS","=","(","name",":","string",")",":","boolean","=>","/","\\.mdx?$","/","iu",".","test","(","name",")","||","name","===","\"",".silo","\""]},"context":{"before":"c4551b94fc49b57a","after":"1f609aa375dcc892"}},"payload":{"text":"What the code alone leaves out: a doc, and silo's records (the ledger's whys, the manifest's whats).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:53.413Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:53.413Z"}
{"id":"483ba8c1-847b-4c1a-8db2-4895be291e4b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/git-refs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b7ca3d8513eff9f85f28e7060d95109bb078e060","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"6de288461c9845a4"}},"payload":{"text":"A commit beside the work, read-only: a branch, tag or commit opened is a folder of the workspace, `.refs/<name>/`, its\nfiles as that commit has them, read from git's objects — no copy in the workspace's store. It's how a removed\nfeature's code is read at its tombstone, and the rewrite's Measure reads `full-editor` (ARCHITECTURE.md, *The\nrewrite, in place*). The Explorer, Quick Open, Find in Files and agents' files_* read it as any folder; git doesn't\nsee it (it reads the store), nor does TypeScript's project (a dot-folder), and the walks for the project's manifests\nleave it out (editor-api's `REFS_DIR`). Nothing is written there: a write is refused, not let fall through to the workspace.\n\n- the command `editor.git.openRef` (\"Git: Open a Commit Read-Only…\"): a branch, tag or commit, fetched one commit deep\nwhen the clone hasn't it, then shown in the Explorer;\n- `git.openRef` { ref, stripped? }: the same, for agents' `git_open`.\n\nOr with its comments stripped, at `.refs/<name>~stripped/`: the code alone, as the rewrite's zero-knowledge pass reads\nit (ARCHITECTURE.md, *What's self-explanatory*) — each code file with its comments blanked by BABLR (bablr.ts' `stripped`,\nline for line the file as it is), and no docs: no Markdown, no `.silo/`.\n\nOpen until the window reloads.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:21.422Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:21.422Z"}
{"id":"50c8100c-8069-4378-b530-3e9f2adbe882","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1f609aa375dcc892","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/git-refs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7e78daeea0e525e7b68b728c81e544623a4ba220","start":2867,"end":3047},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","refused","(","path",":","string",")",":","FileSystemProviderError","{","return","FileSystemProviderError",".","create","(","`","","${","path","}"," is a commit's, read-only","`",",","FileSystemProviderErrorCode",".","FileWriteLocked",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"c987c4e2850e5c02","after":"aa49aeec36b8b75d"}},"payload":{"text":"A write somewhere under `.refs/`, refused — an error the overlay doesn't pass on to the workspace's provider.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:49.988Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:49.988Z"}
